-# of them is in this file so far.
+# The base images are build arguments rather than literals, which is the convention the first project's
+# container step established and the reason is the machine rather than taste: behind a registry mirror
+# `rust:1.98-alpine` is stored as `docker.1ms.run/library/rust:1.98-alpine`, and a literal `FROM` would
+# not find it. The `container-repro` gate reads these defaults, resolves each against the local image
+# store, and passes the names this engine actually has back as `--build-arg`. The defaults below are
+# what a machine with Docker Hub access uses.
+#
+# The builder image is pinned to the same compiler as `rust-toolchain.toml`: `rust:1.98-alpine`
+# carries `RUST_VERSION=1.98.1`. That is not a coincidence to rely on — it is the reason the binary
+# built here and the binary built on this machine come from one toolchain (`docs/build.md`).
