+# a second build of the same image copies layers instead of compiling the whole dependency tree again.
+# A mount is not a layer, which is why the binary is copied *out* of this directory below: a build
+# that left its output in the mounted path would hand the next stage an empty file. A Dockerfile that
+# ignored the argument would still build, just without the cache — which is why it is an `ARG` with a
+# default rather than something imposed.
