+# address a client can reach (`127.0.0.1` is "this container only") and a store directory on a volume
+# it may write, so the obvious lines would be `ENV LAKELET_LISTEN_ADDR=0.0.0.0:7000` and an
+# `ENV LAKELET_STORE_DIR=/data`. Neither is here: the `container-repro` gate compares the
+# configuration report the image answers with the report this machine's binary answers, and it copies
+# the image's environment into the host's process only for names in the `MAILER__` namespace — a
+# leftover from the gate being written for the first project. A `LAKELET_*` variable baked into the
+# image is therefore a difference the gate reports as "the image does not run the binary this tree
+# builds", which is true and is not the reason anybody would guess. Environment is the deployment's
+# half of the four layers (`lakelet/4.1-ingest-protocol`): it arrives at `docker run -e …`, and the
+# two variables above are the two a deployment has to supply.
