+## Why this page exists
 
-[TODO](TODO)
+"The build produced this binary" is a claim about a moment. The moment had a compiler, a set of
+dependency versions, a set of options, and a directory — and a claim that does not name all four is
+not something anybody can check. This page is the checkable half of it: two builds of this tree, in
+two different directories, with the same pinned compiler and the same locked dependencies, compared
+byte for byte.
+
+The comparison is a file rather than a paragraph — [scripts/repro.sh](../scripts/repro.sh), run as
+`sh scripts/repro.sh` — for the same reason the pipeline is a file: a procedure somebody has to
+remember is a procedure that gets done differently at 2 a.m. The interpreter is spelled out because
+the file arrives as a patch and a patch carries content rather than a mode bit: `chmod +x` makes it a
+command you can run directly, and `sh` does the same thing for a checkout that never got one. The script copies this tree's sources into two directories of deliberately
+different depth, builds each with `--locked` and the channel [rust-toolchain.toml](../rust-toolchain.toml)
